public import FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster.GeneratedAxisGlobalTwelveTenthForestOps

/-! Data of the bitset certificate for the Eighth binary forest.

The 52 roots are one point of each orbit, on the singular binary masks, of the group generated
by the sixteen Eighth letters (twelve Golay basis signs and two explicit flag-stabilizer
permutation words with their inverses): 37 type-four orbits, Ω first, and 15 short classes and
zero. The 25 doubling steps are words in the letters together with row operations computing
the binary matrix of each word. All data are discovery outputs; the kernel checks every use. -/

@[expose] public section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster

/-- Row-operation validity is decidable. -/
instance eighthForestRowValidDecidable (o : ℕ × ℕ) : Decidable (TenthForestRowValid o) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∧ _))

